Feature: Closing-ceremony lean pass

  # BL-820 (slice 2 of BL-818). At shift close a named lean step runs: the
  # coordinator brings a shift-scoped packet folded from BL-819's lifecycle
  # ledger, may act within powers it already holds, and hands the packet to the
  # specifier — who turns it into a process ticket, a spec/gate tweak, or an
  # explicit reasoned no-change. The human's words: "a silent ceremony is a
  # failed ceremony." The packet reaches the specifier, not only the briefing.
  #
  # PARKED AS .feature.draft per BL-233: this slice is not built and is
  # additionally blocked on a shift-close hook that does not exist yet
  # (depends_on BL-762). A live *.feature here would have no step handlers and
  # would hard-fail the acceptance runner for every other ticket. The coder
  # renames this to .feature and lands its step handlers in the same parcel.

  Background:
    Given a shift with a lifecycle ledger holding that shift's tickets

  # BL-820 ceremony-actually-invoked-at-shift-close-01
  Scenario: the shift-close path invokes the lean pass as a named step
    When the shift-close path reaches its lean step
    Then the coordinator+specifier lean pass is invoked
    And the pass runs before the shift fully winds down

  # BL-820 packet-is-shift-scoped-evidence-not-a-log-dump-02
  Scenario: the packet carries shift-scoped findings, never raw logs
    When the coordinator builds the closing packet
    Then it names the path taken, dwell hotspots, bounce classes, skip reasons, and stalls for that shift
    And it carries between one and three concrete process hypotheses
    And it contains no raw log transcript

  # BL-820 packet-covers-only-its-own-shift-03
  Scenario: the packet excludes tickets from other shifts
    Given the ledger also holds entries from the previous shift
    When the coordinator builds the closing packet
    Then only the current shift's lifecycle entries are summarised

  # BL-820 specifier-produces-an-outcome-04
  Scenario Outline: the specifier turns the packet into a recorded outcome
    Given the specifier receives the closing packet
    When it completes the lean pass with <outcome>
    Then that outcome is recorded against the ceremony run
    And the ceremony run counts as complete

    Examples:
      | outcome                  |
      | a new process ticket     |
      | a spec or gate tweak     |
      | an explicit no-change    |

  # BL-820 silent-ceremony-is-a-failure-05
  Scenario: a ceremony that produces nothing is recorded as failed
    Given the specifier receives the closing packet
    When the lean pass ends without any recorded outcome
    Then the ceremony run is recorded as failed
    And that failure is surfaced rather than passed over silently

  # BL-820 packet-reaches-specifier-not-only-briefing-06
  Scenario: the packet reaches the specifier's work loop
    When the coordinator builds the closing packet
    Then the packet is delivered to the specifier
    And delivery does not depend on the human reading the briefing

  # BL-820 coordinator-within-power-adjustments-recorded-07
  Scenario: within-power adjustments are recorded, and nothing beyond them is taken
    Given the packet shows a dwell hotspot the coordinator can act on
    When the coordinator makes a within-power adjustment
    Then the adjustment is limited to promotion order or throttle posture
    And the adjustment is recorded against the ceremony run
    And no domain spec is authored and no constitution article is edited

  # BL-820 tentative-adjustments-are-reversible-08
  Scenario: a tentative adjustment is ticketed or noted, never a silent edit
    Given the lean pass proposes a process adjustment
    When that adjustment is applied
    Then it is either ticketed or recorded as a note
    And it is reversible from that record alone

  # BL-820 mid-shift-digest-does-not-replace-the-pass-09
  Scenario: a mid-shift digest does not satisfy the end-of-shift pass
    Given a mid-shift bounce digest already reached the specifier
    When the shift-close path reaches its lean step
    Then the closing lean pass still runs
    And the mid-shift digest is not accepted in its place

  # BL-820 empty-shift-still-produces-an-explicit-no-change-10
  Scenario: a shift with no lifecycle activity still ends in an explicit outcome
    Given a shift whose ledger holds no ticket lifecycle entries
    When the closing lean pass runs
    Then it records an explicit no-change outcome
    And the ceremony run counts as complete
